1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
The record says: 5 kg atta sales down 59% week on week. What actually happened: the shelf was empty for 39 open hours.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:09,300
A supermarket in Bengaluru, June 2026. A synthetic world with an answer key, read the way a data team reads it.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:15,700
Monday’s dashboard: 5 kg atta sales down 59%, availability 97%. 11 of 12 data tests passed.

4
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:22,100
Asked why, the AI assistant, given the warehouse schema, blames shoppers switching to other packs.

5
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:29,000
What happened: 14 cases behind the rice. The shelf was empty 39 open hours while the books showed 56.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,900
A gap detector on the till lines flags the silence at 19:00 on Wednesday, three open hours in. 6 of its 10 alerts were real.

7
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:42,300
Unconstrain demand and the forecast holds: 25.6 bags a day, not 20.2. Shoppers came for 24.9.

8
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,700
Give the assistant a domain layer: 7 of 7 answers right, not 1. It finds the empty shelf.

9
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:54,600
Rerun June with a shelf check at each alert: 35 bags lost instead of 157.

10
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:59,600
Sales are not demand. And book stock is a belief, not the shelf.
